  "description": "Memory-circle save popup: eight-update opening, a cursor cycle, cancellation fade and restored slot list.",
  "registration": "Both starts are free control at the same activated memory circle. Open Save and the empty-slot list normally, skipping native storage waits. Register the confirmation input once: native update 149 (menu clock 129) corresponds to source VI 301 (UI clock 38385), both phase 9 modulo 24. Apply cancellation 32 updates later on both sides and compare all 48 consecutive frames without seeking. Lossless RGB video timestamps map the source frames from VI 0. All frames check the whole image, complete popup region, menu focus, selected slot, logical confirmation and retained popup content/opacity. Audio is file-only and has no acceptance gate in this case. Set the shared UI presentation origin once to 38236: observed source VI 301 has UI clock 38385 and pairs native update 149. Every one of this case's 48 frame observations yields the same source-UI-minus-native-update constant. The runtime already used the shared UI clock before the first cleanup; the former fixture registered only the local menu clock. No per-frame clock adjustment, capture movement, source substitution or relaxed gate is applied.",
